.TH VIPER4LINUX-CTL 1 "November 2026" "ViPER4Linux-RE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viper4linux-ctl \- inspect and adjust ViPER4Linux-RE's live PipeWire DSP controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viper4linux-ctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ...]
.br
.B viper4linux-ctl --help
.br
.B v4l-cli
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viper4linux-ctl
operates the active per-user ViPER4Linux-RE DSP control channel.
The shorter
.B v4l-cli
command is a symlink for viper4linux-ctl and accepts identical arguments.
Effect commands require an active channel; they do not start PipeWire.
Successful edits are written to the same per-user settings used by the GUI,
including when the GUI is closed. The GUI also reads the live controls while it
is open. Named presets and impulse-response file selection are GUI features,
not CLI features.
.PP
Throughout this manual, a range such as "0 through 100" includes both ends.
A 
.B whole number
has no fractional part (for example, 3 or 3.0). Where a command accepts
.B decimals and rounds,
the value must lie within the stated inclusive range, and the command uses
nearest-integer rounding with halfway values rounded away from zero.
Some controls use fractional internal units instead; those are described
individually. Invalid values return exit status 2 and leave the setting
unchanged. The six numbered command sections follow the GUI tabs in order;
within each section, letters identify individual effect groups.
To see compact command help, use
.BR --help .
.SH COMMAND SEQUENCES
Multiple CLI commands may be supplied in one invocation, separated by spaces.
Each command consumes its documented number of arguments; quote names with
spaces as usual in the shell. Example:
.PP
.B v4l-cli on bass-on psycho-off bass-gain 2.5
.PP
All commands and numeric arguments are validated before any changes are
applied; an invalid argument anywhere in the sequence prevents earlier
changes from being applied. Preset names and saved curves are also validated
before an attached DSP channel is modified. Valid commands execute in their
listed order using the same handlers as standalone commands, and each prints
its usual output. Runtime errors (such as a settings-write failure or backend
shutdown) can still stop the sequence after earlier commands have succeeded:
command sequences are not transactions and do not support rollback.
.PP
.B status --full
may appear in a sequence, as may
.BR eq-presets .
.SH GLOBAL COMMANDS AND BACKEND STATUS
.TP
.B status
Print the six-section live DSP summary, showing effect states, principal
parameters, sample rate, backend PID, and audio-block counter. This summary
does not list every EQ band or every compressor parameter.
.TP
.B status --full
Print the expanded six-section report with all active graphic EQ band
frequencies and levels, each Dynamic EQ band, all multiband compressor
settings, selected EQ preset, and chosen DDC/Convolver files when recorded.
Both status modes are read-only.
The status command never changes or saves settings. A started backend with no
DSP channel reports READY TO PROCESS AUDIO. A connected channel does not prove
that audible music is playing; compare the counter between repeated queries.
.TP
.B on
Enable master DSP processing. No arguments. Prints only the confirmation
.B "Master processing: ON"
instead of the complete status report. The limiter remains in the path.
.TP
.B off
Bypass master DSP processing. No arguments. Prints only the confirmation
.B "Master processing: BYPASSED"
instead of the complete status report. The limiter remains in the path.
.TP
.BR all-on " and " all-off
Backward-compatible aliases for the global
.B on
and
.B off
commands, respectively. No arguments. They also print only the one-line
master-processing confirmation.
.SH "1. OUTPUT"
.SS "A. Master Limiter"
.TP
.BI "limiter-threshold " VALUE
Set limiter threshold. VALUE accepts decimals from 0.3 through 1 inclusive
as a linear multiplier; the DSP stores thousandths. The limiter itself is
always present and has no enable/disable command.
.TP
.BI "limiter-gain " VALUE
Set limiter output gain. VALUE accepts decimals from 0.01 through 2
inclusive as a linear multiplier, stored in hundredths (1.0 is 100%).
.TP
.BI "limiter-pan " VALUE
Set output pan. VALUE accepts decimals from -1 through 1 inclusive,
where -1 is full left, 0 is centered, and 1 is full right; stored in
hundredths.
.SS "B. Playback Gain Control (AGC)"
.TP
.BR agc-on " and " agc-off
Enable or disable Automatic Gain Control. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "agc-strength " VALUE
Set AGC strength. VALUE accepts decimals from 0.5 through 3 inclusive,
stored in hundredths.
.TP
.BI "agc-max " VALUE
Set AGC maximum gain. VALUE accepts decimals from 1 through 10
inclusive, stored in hundredths.
.TP
.BI "agc-threshold " VALUE
Set AGC threshold as a linear multiplier. VALUE accepts decimals from
0.3 through 1 inclusive, stored in thousandths.
.SS "C. LUFS Targeting"
.TP
.BR lufs-on " and " lufs-off
Enable or disable LUFS Targeting. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "lufs-target " VALUE
Set target loudness. VALUE accepts decimals from -24 through -8 LUFS
inclusive, stored in tenths.
.TP
.BI "lufs-max " VALUE
Set maximum LUFS gain adjustment. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through
12 dB inclusive, stored in tenths.
.TP
.BI "lufs-speed " SPEED
Set loudness adaptation speed. SPEED must be the whole number 0 (Slow),
1 (Normal), or 2 (Fast); fractions are rejected.
.SH "2. BASS"
.SS "A. ViPER Bass"
.TP
.BR bass-on " and " bass-off
Enable or disable ViPER Bass only, without changing the master switch.
No arguments.
.TP
.BR bass-toggle " and " toggle
Switch ViPER Bass between enabled and disabled; the latter is a legacy alias.
No arguments.
.TP
.BI "bass-mode " MODE
Choose Bass mode. MODE must be a whole number: 0 = Natural,
1 = Pure Bass+, or 2 = Subwoofer.
.TP
.BI "bass-gain " VALUE
Set ViPER Bass gain. VALUE accepts decimals from 0.5 through 10 inclusive;
it is rounded to the nearest hundredth of a gain unit for DSP storage.
The GUI represents gain in tenths.
.TP
.BI "bass-freq " VALUE
Set ViPER Bass frequency in hertz. VALUE accepts decimals from 15 through
150 inclusive and is rounded to the nearest whole hertz.
.SS "B. ViPER Bass Mono"
.TP
.BR mono-on " and " mono-off
Enable or disable the independent Bass Mono effect. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "mono-mode " VALUE
Choose Bass Mono mode. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 2 inclusive
and is rounded to the nearest whole-number mode: 0 = Natural,
1 = Pure Bass+, or 2 = Subwoofer.
.TP
.BI "mono-strength " VALUE
Set Bass Mono strength. VALUE accepts decimals from 0.5 through 10 inclusive;
the DSP stores hundredths and the GUI displays tenths.
.TP
.BI "mono-freq " VALUE
Set Bass Mono frequency. VALUE accepts decimals from 15 through 150 hertz
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole hertz.
.SS "C. Psychoacoustic Bass"
.TP
.BR psycho-on " and " psycho-off
Enable or disable psychoacoustic bass. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "psycho-cutoff " VALUE
Set cutoff frequency. VALUE accepts decimals from 60 through 150 hertz
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole hertz.
.TP
.BI "psycho-intensity " VALUE
Set effect intensity. VALUE accepts whole numbers or decimals between 0
and 100 inclusive, representing a percentage; decimals are rounded to the
nearest whole percentage point. Example:
.B viper4linux-ctl psycho-intensity 30
.TP
.BI "psycho-order " VALUE
Set harmonic order. VALUE accepts decimals from 2 through 5 inclusive,
rounded to the nearest whole-number order.
.TP
.BI "psycho-original " VALUE
Set the percentage of the unprocessed signal retained by the psychoacoustic
bass processor. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through
100 percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.SS "D. Dynamic System"
The X and Y values are Dynamic System's native shaping parameters, not
frequencies or decibel values. Adjust them together with the strength and
side-contribution controls; the GUI offers the same parameters.
.TP
.BR dynamic-on " and " dynamic-off
Enable or disable Dynamic System bass. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-x-low " VALUE
Set the low X parameter. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 2400
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole unit.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-x-high " VALUE
Set the high X parameter. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 12000
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole unit.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-y-low " VALUE
Set the low Y parameter. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 200
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole unit.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-y-high " VALUE
Set the high Y parameter. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 300
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole unit.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-side-low " VALUE
Set low-side contribution. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100
percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-side-high " VALUE
Set high-side contribution. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100
percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "dynamic-strength " VALUE
Set Dynamic System strength. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100
percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.SH "3. EQ & TONE"
.SS "A. Graphic Equalizer"
Built-in curves are identical to the GUI's original curves at each band
count. User presets are loaded from the GUI's EQ preset library; presets for
a different band count are log-frequency interpolated as in the GUI.
.TP
.B eq-presets
List available built-in and user EQ presets. Works even if the DSP backend
is stopped. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "eq-preset " NAME
Apply a built-in or user EQ preset to the live EQ and save its selection.
Names containing spaces must be quoted. A unique bare name is accepted;
use builtin:NAME or user:NAME to resolve ambiguous names. Custom restores
the saved custom curve for the current band layout. This does not enable
the EQ automatically. No presets are overwritten.
.TP
.BR eq-on " and " eq-off
Enable or disable the graphic equalizer. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "eq-bands " COUNT
Set the number of graphic-EQ bands. COUNT must be exactly one of the whole
numbers 10, 15, 25 or 31. This selects the active EQ layout and marks the EQ preset as Custom.
.TP
.BI "eq-level " "BAND DB"
Set an individual EQ band. BAND must be a whole-number index from 1 through
the current number of bands, inclusive. DB accepts decimals from -12 through
+12 dB inclusive, stored to the nearest hundredth of a decibel.
Changing a band marks the EQ preset as Custom; built-in preset curves remain
unchanged. Example:
.B viper4linux-ctl eq-level 3 -1.75
.SS "B. Dynamic EQ"
.TP
.BR deq-on " and " deq-off
Enable or disable Dynamic EQ. No arguments. Configure individual Dynamic EQ
bands in the GUI.
.SS "C. ViPER Clarity"
.TP
.BR clarity-on " and " clarity-off
Enable or disable ViPER Clarity. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "clarity-gain " VALUE
Set Clarity gain. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 4.5 inclusive;
the DSP stores thousandths and the GUI displays tenths.
.TP
.BI "clarity-mode " VALUE
Select Clarity mode. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 2 inclusive,
rounded to the nearest whole-number mode (0 = Natural, 1 = Ozone, 2 = XHiFi).
.SS "D. Spectrum Extension"
.TP
.BR spectrum-on " and " spectrum-off
Enable or disable Spectrum Extension. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "spectrum-freq " VALUE
Set the reference frequency. VALUE accepts decimals from 2200 through
8200 hertz inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole hertz. The GUI displays
hundreds of hertz.
.TP
.BI "spectrum-exciter " VALUE
Set the harmonic exciter. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 6
inclusive; the DSP stores thousandths and the GUI displays tenths.
.SS "E. Tube Simulator"
.TP
.BR tube-on " and " tube-off
Enable or disable Tube Simulator. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "tube-model " MODE
Set tube type. MODE must be a whole number: 0 = 12AX7, 1 = 12AU7,
or 2 = 6N1P.
.TP
.BI "tube-drive " VALUE
Set tube drive. VALUE must be a whole-number percentage from 0 through
100 inclusive; fractional values are rejected.
.TP
.BI "tube-mix " VALUE
Set tube mix. VALUE must be a whole-number percentage from 0 through
100 inclusive; fractional values are rejected.
.SS "F. AnalogX"
.TP
.BR analogx-on " and " analogx-off
Enable or disable AnalogX. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "analogx-mode " MODE
Choose AnalogX intensity. MODE must be a whole number: 0 = Mild,
1 = Medium, or 2 = Strong.
.SH "4. SPATIAL"
.SS "A. Crossfeed (ViPER Cure)"
.TP
.BR crossfeed-on " and " crossfeed-off
Enable or disable native Cure/Crossfeed. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "crossfeed-mode " MODE
Choose crossfeed preset. MODE must be a whole number: 0 = Mild,
1 = Medium, or 2 = Strong.
.SS "B. Headphone Surround+"
.TP
.BR headphone-on " and " headphone-off
Enable or disable Headphone Surround+. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "headphone-level " LEVEL
Set Headphone Surround+ level. LEVEL must be a whole number from 1 through
5 inclusive, matching the GUI. Decimal fractions are rejected.
.SS "C. Differential Surround"
.TP
.BR diff-on " and " diff-off
Enable or disable Differential Surround. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "diff-delay " VALUE
Set the differential delay. VALUE accepts decimals from 1 through
20 milliseconds inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole millisecond.
.TP
.BI "diff-reverse " FLAG
Set reversed delay routing. FLAG must be the whole number 0 (normal)
or 1 (reversed). Fractions are rejected.
.TP
.BI "diff-mix " VALUE
Set delayed-channel mix. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through
100 percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "diff-lowpass " VALUE
Set differential low-pass frequency. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through
20000 hertz inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole hertz; 0 disables the
low-pass. The GUI represents this control in 100 Hz steps.
.SS "D. Field Surround"
.TP
.BR field-on " and " field-off
Enable or disable Field Surround. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "field-widen " VALUE
Set widening. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 8 inclusive,
stored in tenths.
.TP
.BI "field-mid " VALUE
Set mid-image factor. VALUE accepts decimals from 1 through 2 inclusive,
stored in hundredths.
.TP
.BI "field-depth " VALUE
Set depth contribution. VALUE accepts 0 (depth component disabled) or
decimals from 200 through 950 inclusive; nonzero values are rounded to the
nearest whole unit. Use field-off to disable the entire Field Surround effect.
The GUI exposes coarser 50-unit steps.
.SS "E. Reverberation"
.TP
.BR reverb-on " and " reverb-off
Enable or disable reverberation. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "reverb-room " VALUE
Set room size. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100 percent inclusive,
rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "reverb-width " VALUE
Set stereo width. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100 percent inclusive,
rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "reverb-damp " VALUE
Set damping. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100 percent inclusive,
rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "reverb-wet " VALUE
Set processed (wet) mix. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100 percent
inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.TP
.BI "reverb-dry " VALUE
Set unprocessed (dry) mix. VALUE accepts decimals from 0 through 100
percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.SS "F. Stereo Imager"
.TP
.BR imager-on " and " imager-off
Enable or disable Stereo Imager. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "imager-low " VALUE
Set low-band width. VALUE must be a whole-number percentage from 0 through
200 inclusive; fractional values are rejected. 100 means unchanged width.
.TP
.BI "imager-mid " VALUE
Set mid-band width. VALUE must be a whole-number percentage from 0 through
200 inclusive; fractional values are rejected. 100 means unchanged width.
.TP
.BI "imager-high " VALUE
Set high-band width. VALUE must be a whole-number percentage from 0 through
200 inclusive; fractional values are rejected. 100 means unchanged width.
.TP
.BI "imager-xover-low " VALUE
Set low crossover frequency. VALUE must be a whole number between 80 and
400 hertz inclusive; fractional values are rejected.
.TP
.BI "imager-xover-high " VALUE
Set high crossover frequency. VALUE must be a whole number between 2000 and
8000 hertz inclusive; fractional values are rejected.
.SH "5. DYNAMICS"
.SS "A. FET Compressor"
.TP
.BR fet-on " and " fet-off
Enable or disable FET Compressor. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "fet-threshold " VALUE
Set FET threshold. VALUE must be a whole number from -48 through 0 dB
inclusive; fractional values are rejected.
.TP
.BI "fet-ratio " VALUE
Set FET compression ratio. VALUE accepts decimals from 1 through 10
inclusive, stored in tenths, representing ratios from 1:1 through 10:1.
.SS "B. Multiband Compressor"
.TP
.BR mb-on " and " mb-off
Enable or disable Multiband Compressor. No arguments.
.TP
.BI "mb-bands " COUNT
Set multiband count. COUNT must be the whole number 3 or 5; fractional
values and other whole numbers are rejected. Configure individual band
parameters in the GUI.
.SH "6. SOUND CORRECTION"
.SS "A. ViPER-DDC"
.TP
.BR ddc-on " and " ddc-off
Enable or disable ViPER-DDC correction. No arguments. The selected VDC
profile is managed in the GUI; a valid profile and supported sample rate
are still required.
.SS "B. Speaker Correction"
.TP
.BR speaker-on " and " speaker-off
Enable or disable native Speaker Correction. No arguments.
.SS "C. Convolver"
.TP
.BR convolver-on " and " convolver-off
Enable or disable the convolver. No arguments. Import and select an IRS
or supported WAV impulse response in the GUI.
.TP
.BI "convolver-cross " VALUE
Set the percentage of cross-channel convolution mixing. This control is
separate from the wet/dry settings of other effects. VALUE accepts decimals
from 0 through 100 percent inclusive, rounded to the nearest whole percentage point.
.SH SETTINGS AND PRECISION
CLI edits are applied to the live control channel, then saved to the GUI's
per-user Qt settings store. The short-lived CLI tool reports a nonzero exit
status if settings cannot be written, but audio processing might already have
changed. The GUI polls the backend approximately every 500 milliseconds. A live change
may therefore be visible in the DSP before it appears in the GUI.
.PP
Some CLI parameters accept finer precision than the GUI sliders. While the
backend is running, the live DSP retains the requested value. A later GUI
interaction or complete backend restart may quantize settings to the GUI's
coarser resolution, such as tenths of gain, hundreds of hertz for certain
frequency sliders, or 50-unit Field Depth steps. Use the GUI for fully
round-trippable values when this distinction matters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully, including a read-only status query when
the backend is ready but the DSP channel has not yet appeared.
.TP
.B 1
Backend or DSP control unavailable for the requested command, or a settings
persistence failure after a live control change.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command, wrong number of arguments, or invalid value, once the DSP
control channel is available. Backend availability is checked first, so an
unavailable backend can produce exit status 1 even for an invalid command.
For example,
.B viper4linux-ctl tube-drive 12.5
is rejected because tube-drive requires a whole number, whereas
.B viper4linux-ctl psycho-intensity 12.5
is accepted and rounded to 13.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B viper4linux-ctl status
Inspect current DSP state without modifying it.
.TP
.B viper4linux-ctl bass-on
Enable Bass while leaving master processing unchanged.
.TP
.B viper4linux-ctl clarity-gain 2.5
Set Clarity gain to 2.5.
.TP
.B viper4linux-ctl eq-bands 15
Use the 15-band graphic EQ mode.
.TP
.B viper4linux-ctl eq-level 2 -1.75
Apply -1.75 dB to EQ band 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR viper4linux (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
